# *.sym
All symbol names used by the IR, separated by NUL bytes.  A `sym` is
the byte offset of a name in this file.
Mangled names: user labels are "func.label", static locals are
"func.name", generated labels are ".Ln", switch temporaries are ".swN".

# *.str
All strings from the C file, separated by NUL bytes.

# *.ast
Magic: "CIR\0"

## Misc Stuff
byte:
	8bit integer
word:
	16bit integer, little endian
dword:
	32bit integer, little endian
sym: word
	offset of a name in the symbol file; if the high bit is set,
	the low 15 bits are a generated label number (".LN") and the
	name is not in the symbol file
six: word
	offset into the string file
ty: byte
	The type of an expression, so that c1 knows the width and
	signedness of every operand:
	[1:0]	width: 0 = 1 byte, 1 = word, 2 = dword, 3 = block
	[2]	0 = signed, 1 = unsigned (pointers are unsigned words)
	If the width is block, a word with the byte count follows the
	ty byte.  Blocks only appear as the type of "=" and "*".
	Whenever an operand is narrower than its operation, c1 extends
	it according to the operand's own ty; arguments in a call are
	promoted to at least a word.

## Model
`g` and `l` denote the ADDRESS of an object (a word); `*` loads
through an address, and "=" stores through one.  Reading a variable
is `* (g x)`; an array or function name decays to its address by a
bare `g`/`l`.  Pointer arithmetic has already been scaled to bytes by
c0.  c1 must not evaluate the right side of &&, || and ?: eagerly
(the tags below carry these operators; c1 generates the short
circuit).

## Global Definitions

Data Declaration: "D" flags sym size init? "\x00"
flags (byte):
	[1:0]:	storage class
		0x00: extern	(symbol defined elsewhere)
		0x01: global	(symbol defined in this file)
		0x02: static	(defined here, not exported)
	[2]:	initialized
size (word):
	number of bytes
init: chunk* (exactly `size` bytes; c1 pads with zeros)
	0x01 word-n		followed by n literal bytes
	0x02 sym word-addend	a word holding address of sym + addend
	0x03 six word-addend	a word holding the address of the string
				file entry six + addend
	0x00			end of chunks

Function Declaration: "F" flags sym "\xff"
Function Definition: "F" flags sym code "\xff" args "\xff\xff" vars "\xff\xff"
flags (byte):
	[1:0]:	storage class, see "D"
	[2]:	definition (with code and the lists); without it this
		is a declaration and the rest is omitted
code (stmts):
	The body, streamed in source order, lowered to statements
args (words):
	The sizes of the parameters in bytes, in declaration order;
	the code comes first, so that c0 can write it as it parses
vars (words):
	The sizes of the local auto variables (including hidden
	switch temporaries), in declaration order; `l` indexes into
	the concatenation of args and vars, assigned in declaration
	order as the code is parsed

## Statements (stmt):
Return (no value):	"r"
Return (with value): 	"R" ty expr
	ty is the function's return type; c1 converts the expression
	to it
Label:			"L" sym
Jump:			"J" sym
Branch:			"B" true false cond
	Jump to true (sym) or false (sym), based on cond (expr)
Expr:			"E" expr

## Expressions (expr):
Integer:		"i" ty word
Long:			"I" ty dword
	chosen by ty, or by the value not fitting a word
String:			"S" six
	taken from the .string file
Global Symbol:		"g" ty sym
	the address of sym (a word, unsigned)
Local Symbol:		"l" ty byte
	the address of local slot `byte` (a word, unsigned)
Unary:			"u" ty op expr
	op (byte): '-' | '~' | '!'
Binary:			"b" ty op expr expr
	op (byte): '+' | '-' | '*' | '/' | '%' | '&' | '|' | '^'
		| '<' | '>' | 'L' (<=) | 'G' (>=) | 'E' (==) | 'N' (!=)
		| 'l' (<<) | 'r' (>>) | 'A' (&&) | 'O' (||)
Ternary:		"?" ty cond true false
	Only the selected branch is evaluated.
Call:			"c" ty nargs func args
	nargs (byte):	number of arguments
	func (expr):	the function (its address)
	args (exprs):	the arguments, in source order
Assignment:		"=" ty dest src
	dest (expr):	an address expression ("g", "l", "*" forms)
	src (expr):	the value; for a compound assignment c0 has
			already emitted dest = dest op src
Inc/Dec:		"n" ty op when scale lval
	op (byte):	'+' | '-'
	when (byte):	0 = postfix, 1 = prefix
	scale (word):	the step in bytes (1, or the size of the
			pointed-to object)
	lval (expr):	an address expression
Comma:			"," ty expr expr
	evaluate left, then right; value is the right one
Dereference:		"*" ty expr
	the value at the address; ty is the pointee (or a block)
Address of, casts, member access ".", "->", index "[]" and sizeof
	do not appear: c0 lowers them into the forms above ("&x" is
	just the address expression of x, casts retype a node and
	rely on width reconciliation, "a[i]" is *(a + i*scale), "p->m"
	is *(p + offset)).

# *.ssa
Magic: "CIR\001"

The SSA form uses block arguments instead of phi nodes: a label declares
parameters and every jump/branch binds them by position, like a function call.
This makes the parallel copy a phi would imply explicit on the edge.

## Misc Stuff
reg: word
	Index into the register table.
	-1 (0xffff) means "no value" where a value is optional.
size: byte
	0=byte, 1=word, 2=dword

## Global Definitions

Data Declaration: (see *.ast; passed through unchanged)

Function Declaration: "F" flags sym "\xff"
Function Definition: "F" flags sym args "\xff\xff" vars "\xff\xff" code "\xff" regs "\xff\xff" "\xff"

flags, args, vars: see *.ast
	[1:0]:	storage class, see "D"
	[2]:	definition (with code and the lists); without it this
		is a declaration and the rest is omitted
	args:	word sizes in bytes, in declaration order
	vars:	word sizes in bytes, in declaration order
	`l slot` indexes the concatenation args+vars.
regs (word):
	one entry per SSA value; value ids are 0-based indices.
	[15:14]: byte=00, word=01, dword=10
	[13: 0]: reserved (0); c3 assigns homes itself

## SSA stmts

Label:			"L" sym nparams p0 ... p(nparams-1)
	Declares a block and the values it receives as block arguments.
	Most labels (c0's own control flow) have 0 params; only the synthetic
	merge blocks of &&, || and ?: have 1.
Jump:			"J" sym nargs a0 ... a(nargs-1)
Branch:			"B" cond tsym tn t0... fsym fn f0...
	cond is a value; the true edge binds `tn` args to tsym and the
	false edge binds `fn` args to fsym.
Return (no value):	"r"
Return (with value):	"R" src
Integer:		"i" size dst byte|word|dword
String:			"S" dst six
Global Symbol:		"g" dst sym		(address, a word)
Local Symbol:		"l" dst slot		(address, a word)
Cast:			"C" flags dst src
	flags: 0=truncate, 1=zero-extend, 2=sign-extend
Call:			"c" size nargs dst func (ty arg){nargs}
Store:			"=" size dst src	(dst is an address; [dst] = src)
Load:			"*" size dst src	(dst = [src])
Unary:			"u" size op dst src
Binary:			"b" flags op dst a b
	flags: byte; [1:0] size, [2] signed, [3] b is an immediate
	(nargs, nparams, tn, fn are words, not bytes)
